# 18. CRITICAL USER FLOWS

Phải triển khai tối thiểu các luồng sau:

### Flow A — First Setup

Open App → Create Home → Create Floor → Create Room → Add Device → BLE Configuration hoặc Manual IP → Enter Token → Verify REST API → Name Sensor → Place on Map → Dashboard.

### Flow B — Fire Alarm

ESP32 detects condition → GET status returns ALARM → App updates UI → Notification while monitoring active → User opens map → Correct room highlighted → User acknowledges → Command pending → Event confirms result → Alarm state remains controlled by firmware.

### Flow C — Wi-Fi Relocation

ESP32 becomes unreachable → App shows offline → User selects Reconfigure via BLE → Connects to selected node → Sends new Wi-Fi → Receives new IP → Verifies REST identity → Saves new IP → Resumes monitoring.

### Flow D — Building Setup

Create Home → Define Floors → Add Rooms → Draw/Import Floorplan → Calibrate Dimensions → Mark Nodes → Mark Extinguishers → Mark Exits → Save Map → View Map.

### Flow E — User Position

Open Map → Select current room or scan location QR → App shows manually determined/QR-derived location → Display nearby assets with clear limitations.

### Flow F — AI Insights

Receive real samples → Persist history → Compute local trends → Generate source-backed insight → Display analysis details → Never change firmware alarm policy.

### Flow G — Lost Connection During Alarm

Last known ALARM → Network lost → Keep last known alarm visible with offline indicator → Do not mark NORMAL → Resume connection and verify fresh state.

